he single went straight to the number one position in South Korea."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0280-7683f713116d:d02", "start": 340, "end": 430, "text": "The single and its album launched Rain as an international artist throughout Asia in 2005."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0280-7683f713116d:d02", "start": 431, "end": 542, "text": "Both reached number one in several places, including Vietnam, Taiwan, Thailand, China, Shanghai, and Hong Kong."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0280-7683f713116d:d02", "start": 543, "end": 606, "text": "With this single, Rain presented a brand-new image to his fans,"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0280-7683f713116d:d03", "start": 0, "end": 75, "text": "song was met with commercial success , and topped various domestic charts ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0280-7683f713116d:d03", "start": 76, "end": 219, "text": "It won the Most Popular Music Video daesang award at the 2004 Mnet Km Music Video Festival and the Grand Prize at the annual KBS Music Awards ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0280-7683f713116d:d03", "start": 220, "end": 564, "text": "Contents 1 Background and composition 2 Reception and impact 3 Accolades 4 Music video and live performances 5 Credits and personnel 6 Release history 7 References 8 External links Background and composition edit In an attempt to attract a larger international audience , he changed his name from Bi ( meaning 'rain ' in Korean ) to its English"}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Irma Thomas", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0280-7683f713116d:d00:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "Rain", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0280-7683f713116d:d02:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0280-7683f713116d:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0280-7683f713116d:d00:c0", "entity": "artist", "scope": "song \"It's Raining\"", "claim": "Irma Thomas is the artist of the song \"It's Raining\".", "answer": "Irma Thomas", "quote": "It's Raining (Irma Thomas song) \"It's Raining\" is a soul/R&B ballad, credited as written by Naomi Neville. It was first recorded in November 1961 by Irma Thomas, and produced by Allen Toussaint.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0280-7683f713116d:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0280-7683f713116d:d02:c0", "entity": "artist", "scope": "song \"It's Raining\"", "claim": "Rain is the artist of the song \"It's Raining\".", "answer": "Rain", "quote": "It's Raining (Rain song) \"It's Raining\" is a Korean language song, and the first single from the third album, by Korean R&B singer, Rain.", "original_document_number": 3}], "initial_answers": ["Irma Thomas", "Rain"]}
